      "content": "You can take ibuprofen to help with the throbbing, but do not take it with the antibiotic cream unless you are absolutely sure you have no allergies, as mixing them can cause skin irritation. Yes, this could be cellulitis, but since you are applying the cream and taking the painkiller, you are already treating it aggressively enough to stop it from getting worse. Just keep the area clean and dry, and if the swelling increases tomorrow, you will have to go to the doctor.",
